#: ../../../source/architecture/architecture.rst:13
msgid ""
"The core insight of v0.3 is splitting the old ``AbaqusCalculation`` God-"
"object into two narrow contracts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/architecture/architecture.rst:16
msgid ""
":class:`~ABQflow.JobContext` — **frozen** data: paths, job name, CPU "
"count. Strategies see data, not implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/architecture/architecture.rst:18
msgid ""
":class:`~ABQflow.AbaqusRunner` — a **service** with three public methods:"
" ``run_solver()``, ``run_hook()``, and the internal ``_base_command()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/architecture/architecture.rst:21
msgid ""
"Strategies depend only on ``(ctx, runner, logger)`` — not on "
"``AbaqusCalculation`` private methods.  This eliminates the circular "
"import that required ``TYPE_CHECKING`` hacks, makes strategies "
"independently testable (mock the runner), and gives each layer a clear "
"responsibility."
msgstr ""

